IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc97-nouns`
IMPORT `mc97-status`
IMPORT `mc97-preamble`
IMPORT `mc97-c01`
IMPORT `mc97-c09`
IMPORT `mc97-c29`
IMPORT `mc97-saving`

-- MAGNA CARTA (1297), 1297 c. 9 (25 Edw. 1), from the site's traditional translation -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person asking what Magna Carta (1297) secures them, on the parts of its text that show no repeal annotation:
-- whether the Church of England is free (chapter 1); whether the City of London and other cities, boroughs, towns and the Barons of
-- the Five Ports keep their liberties and free customs (chapter 9); whether they may be taken, imprisoned, disseised, outlawed,
-- exiled or in any way destroyed, or have the King proceed against or condemn them, other than by lawful judgment of their Peers or
-- by the Law of the Land, and whether Justice or Right may be sold, denied or deferred (chapter 29); and what the three paragraphs
-- under the "General Saving" heading promise about the observance of the Liberties.
--
-- This layer asks the questions; every rule it uses is in the layer-1 modules imported above, and nothing here restates one.
-- Each question takes plain inputs (yes/no, or a choice from the text's own words), one per fact the person can state, each with an
-- @desc worded as the person would be asked. The answers are the layer-1 answers, in the layer-1 words:
--   "covered by the text" means the text says so;  "not covered by the text" means the text is SILENT. It does not mean "no".
-- The text does not say whether any of this is, or ever was, in force; no answer here says so (see NOTES.md).
--
-- There is no seat for the King, for his Heirs or for any official. Where a provision is about the King's own acts (chapter 29,
-- "We will not ..."; the promise in the first paragraph), the question is what that means for the person: may it be done to them,
-- is the promise made to them.
--
-- Not asked here, and why: the subsidy in the first paragraph ("have given unto Us the Fifteenth Part of all their Moveables") is a
-- statement of what the named classes gave, not a promise to the person; it is in layer 1 (mc97-saving.l4) and in the cases file. The
-- status entries for the chapters shown repealed (mc97-status.l4) are not questions a person asks of the law either.

§ `Magna Carta (1297) -- what it secures me`

§§ `The preamble: to whom the Liberties following are given`

-- preamble paragraph 2. "Archbishops, Bishops, Abbots, Priors, Earls, Barons, and ... all [Freemen] of this our Realm" are named.
-- A class the paragraph does not name is not addressed by it: the answer for it is "not covered by the text", not "no".
@export Am I among those to whom the Liberties following are given and granted (preamble paragraph 2)?
GIVEN `the capacity I ask in` IS A Capacity @desc In which capacity are you asking? One of: an Archbishop, a Bishop, an Abbot, a Prior, an Earl, a Baron, a Freeman of the Realm, a Templar, a Hospitaller, a Knight, a Freeholder, another Subject, another Person
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Am I among those to whom the Liberties following are given and granted` IS
    `preamble paragraph 2: these Liberties following are given and granted to` `the capacity I ask in`

§§ `Chapter 1: Confirmation of Liberties`

-- chapter 1, first sentence. The only body it names is the Church of England.
@export Is the Church of England free (chapter 1)?
GIVEN `I am asking about the Church of England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body you are asking about the Church of England?
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Is the Church of England free` IS
    `chapter 1: the body shall be free` `the body I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the body I ask about` MEANS
            IF `I am asking about the Church of England`
            THEN `the Church of England`
            ELSE `another body`

@export Does the Church of England have all her whole Rights and Liberties inviolable (chapter 1)?
GIVEN `I am asking about the Church of England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body you are asking about the Church of England?
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Does the Church of England have all her whole Rights and Liberties inviolable` IS
    `chapter 1: the body shall have all her whole Rights and Liberties inviolable` `the body I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the body I ask about` MEANS
            IF `I am asking about the Church of England`
            THEN `the Church of England`
            ELSE `another body`

-- chapter 1, second sentence. "all the Freemen of our Realm" and "their Heirs".
@export Do I hold the Liberties under-written, as a Freeman of the Realm or the Heir of one (chapter 1)?
GIVEN `I am a Freeman of the Realm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Freeman of the Realm?
      `I am an Heir of a Freeman of the Realm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Heir of a Freeman of the Realm?
GIVETH A `Holding under chapter 1`
DECIDE `Do I hold the Liberties under-written` IS
    `chapter 1: how the Liberties under-written are held` `I am a Freeman of the Realm` `I am an Heir of a Freeman of the Realm`

§§ `Chapter 9: Liberties of London, &c.`

-- chapter 9. The answer is in the text's own words.
@export What does chapter 9 say my City, Borough, Town or Port shall have (chapter 9)?
GIVEN `the community I belong to` IS A Community @desc What are you, or what do you belong to? One of: the City of London, another City, a Borough, a Town, a Baron of the Five Ports, another Port, a community of another kind
GIVETH A `Chapter 9 entitlement`
DECIDE `What does chapter 9 say my community shall have` IS
    `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `the community I belong to`

@export Does my community keep this Liberty or Custom (chapter 9)?
GIVEN `the community I belong to` IS A Community @desc What are you, or what do you belong to? One of: the City of London, another City, a Borough, a Town, a Baron of the Five Ports, another Port, a community of another kind
      `it is a Custom, not a Liberty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you ask about a Custom (answer no if it is a Liberty)?
      `it is old` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it old? (Asked of the City of London only.)
      `my community hath been used to have it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Hath your community been used to have it? (Asked of the City of London only.)
      `it is my community's own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it your own community's Liberty or Custom? (Asked of every community but the City of London.)
      `the Custom is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a Custom: is it a free Custom? (Asked of every community but the City of London.)
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Does my community keep this Liberty or Custom` IS
    `chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` `the community I belong to` `the kind of thing` `it is old` `my community hath been used to have it` `it is my community's own` `the Custom is free`
    WHERE
        `the kind of thing` MEANS
            IF `it is a Custom, not a Liberty`
            THEN `a Custom`
            ELSE `a Liberty`

§§ `Chapter 29: only if something has been done, or may be done, to you`

-- chapter 29, first sentence. Ask this group only of a person to whom one of the listed things has happened or is threatened.
-- "Freeman", "lawful judgment of his Peers" and "the Law of the Land" are not defined by the text; the person states each.
@export May I be taken, imprisoned, disseised, outlawed, exiled, destroyed, passed upon or condemned, other than by lawful judgment of my Peers or by the Law of the Land (chapter 29)?
GIVEN `I am a Freeman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Freeman?
      `what is done or threatened to me` IS A Treatment @desc What is done, or threatened, to you? One of: taken, imprisoned, disseised of his Freehold, disseised of his Liberties, disseised of his free Customs, outlawed, exiled, any other wise destroyed, passed upon, condemned, some other treatment
      `there was a lawful judgment of my Peers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a lawful judgment of your Peers?
      `it is done by the Law of the Land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by the Law of the Land?
GIVETH A `Chapter 29 outcome`
DECIDE `May I be taken, imprisoned or condemned other than by lawful judgment of my Peers or the Law of the Land` IS
    `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` `I am a Freeman` `what is done or threatened to me` `there was a lawful judgment of my Peers` `it is done by the Law of the Land`

-- chapter 29, first sentence. Who the text says would do it.
@export Does chapter 29 say who would do it to me (chapter 29)?
GIVEN `what is done or threatened to me` IS A Treatment @desc What is done, or threatened, to you? One of: taken, imprisoned, disseised of his Freehold, disseised of his Liberties, disseised of his free Customs, outlawed, exiled, any other wise destroyed, passed upon, condemned, some other treatment
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
DECIDE `Does chapter 29 say who would do it to me` IS
    `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `what is done or threatened to me`

-- chapter 29, last sentence. "any man" and "no man": not "Freeman".
@export May Justice or Right be sold to me, denied me or deferred to me (chapter 29)?
GIVEN `I am a man in the text's sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a "man" in the text's sense of "any man" (the text does not define it)?
      `what is at stake` IS A `Thing dealt in` @desc What is at stake? One of: Justice, Right, another thing
GIVETH A `Chapter 29 outcome`
DECIDE `May Justice or Right be sold to me, denied me or deferred to me` IS
    `chapter 29, last sentence: selling, denying or deferring` `I am a man in the text's sense` `what is at stake`

§§ `The General Saving: the paragraphs after chapter 37`

-- first paragraph, the reservation. "all Persons, as well Spiritual as Temporal".
@export Are my free Liberties and free Customs, which I have had in time passed, reserved to me (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Liberty or Custom you ask about a free one?
      `I have had it in time passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had it in time passed?
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Are my free Liberties and free Customs reserved to me` IS
    `first paragraph: the reservation reserves` `it is free` `I have had it in time passed`

@export How does the reservation reach me (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `the capacity I ask in` IS A Capacity @desc In which capacity are you asking? One of: an Archbishop, a Bishop, an Abbot, a Prior, an Earl, a Baron, a Freeman of the Realm, a Templar, a Hospitaller, a Knight, a Freeholder, another Subject, another Person
GIVETH A `How a capacity is reached`
DECIDE `How does the reservation reach me` IS
    `first paragraph: how the reservation reaches` `the capacity I ask in`

-- first paragraph, "all Men of this our Realm ... shall observe the same against all Persons".
@export Must I observe these Customs and Liberties against all Persons (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `I am a Man of this our Realm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Man of this our Realm, whether Spiritual or Temporal?
      `observing lies within my power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does observing them lie within your power?
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Must I observe these Customs and Liberties` IS
    `first paragraph: a Man of the Realm shall observe` `I am a Man of this our Realm` `observing lies within my power`

-- first paragraph, "we shall observe". The King's own duty, asked for what it means to the person: does the King owe observance of this?
@export Is the King bound to observe this Custom or Liberty, as much as appertains to him and his Heirs (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `it is one of the Customs and Liberties granted in this Charter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it one of the Customs and Liberties the Charter grants to be holden within the Realm?
      `it appertains to the King and his Heirs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appertain to the King and his Heirs?
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Is the King bound to observe this Custom or Liberty` IS
    `first paragraph: the King shall observe` `it is one of the Customs and Liberties granted in this Charter` `it appertains to the King and his Heirs`

-- first paragraph, the promise "granted unto them on the other part".
@export Was the King's promise not to infringe the Liberties granted to me (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `the capacity I ask in` IS A Capacity @desc In which capacity are you asking? One of: an Archbishop, a Bishop, an Abbot, a Prior, an Earl, a Baron, a Freeman of the Realm, a Templar, a Hospitaller, a Knight, a Freeholder, another Subject, another Person
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Was the King's promise not to infringe the Liberties granted to me` IS
    `first paragraph: the promise is granted unto` `the capacity I ask in`

@export May the King or his Heir procure or do a thing that infringes or breaks the Liberties (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `the one who would procure or do it` IS A Party @desc Who would procure or do it? One of: the King, an Heir of the King, a Man of the Realm
      `it infringes or breaks the Liberties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it infringe or break the Liberties in this Charter contained?
GIVETH A Prohibition
DECIDE `May the King or his Heir procure or do a thing that infringes the Liberties` IS
    `first paragraph: the King and his Heirs shall not procure or do` `the one who would procure or do it` `it infringes or breaks the Liberties`

-- first paragraph, "of no force nor effect".
@export Is a thing procured contrary to these Liberties of any force or effect (first paragraph)?
GIVEN `it was procured by any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it procured by any person?
      `it is contrary to the Liberties and the promises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it contrary to the Liberties in this Charter and what the paragraph has promised?
GIVETH A Effect
DECIDE `Is a thing procured contrary to these Liberties of any force or effect` IS
    `first paragraph: a thing procured` `it was procured by any person` `it is contrary to the Liberties and the promises`

-- second paragraph.
@export Must the Charter and its Articles be observed for ever (second paragraph)?
GIVEN `it is this Charter or one of its Articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you ask about the Charter or one of its Articles?
GIVETH A Coverage
DECIDE `Must the Charter and its Articles be observed for ever` IS
    `second paragraph: the Charter and its Articles shall be observed for ever` `it is this Charter or one of its Articles`

@export Does the second paragraph command that an Article not yet kept be observed from henceforth (second paragraph)?
GIVEN `it is an Article of the same Charter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an Article of the same Charter?
      `it hath hitherto been kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Hath it hitherto been kept?
GIVETH A Command
DECIDE `Does the second paragraph command that an Article not yet kept be observed from henceforth` IS
    `second paragraph: an Article that hath not been kept` `it is an Article of the same Charter` `it hath hitherto been kept`

@export Has the King confirmed, made strong and renewed this gift or grant (second paragraph)?
GIVEN `the gift or grant I ask about` IS A `Gift or grant` @desc Which gift or grant? One of: the grant of the Liberties to the classes of preamble paragraph 2, the grant of the Liberties to the Freemen of chapter 1, the gift of the Fifteenth Part of Moveables, the grant that neither We nor our Heirs shall procure an infringement, a gift or grant this text does not show
GIVETH A Confirmation
DECIDE `Has the King confirmed, made strong and renewed this gift or grant` IS
    `second paragraph: what is confirmed, made strong and renewed` `the gift or grant I ask about`
